  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#building-paths\n\n> If the last subpath had more than one point in its list of points, then this is equivalent to adding a straight line connecting the last point back to the first point, thus \"closing\" the shape, and then repeating the last (possibly implied) moveTo() call.\n\nThere is a confusion about how this shall behave at https://code.google.com/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=552080#c6 \n\nShall the following code produce two  (because last moveTo part of the path) or three (because last moveTo is not \"played\" until closePath is applied) lines?\n\n```\nctx.moveTo(9.8255,71.1829);\nctx.lineTo(103,25);\nctx.lineTo(118,25);\nctx.moveTo(9.8255,71.1829);\nctx.closePath();\nctx.stroke();\n```\n",
